# Known oracle defect, not a rustdl finding (#363 step 3, control case 83, shrunk).
# Reflexive(r0) makes r0(x,x) hold for every x; Asymmetric(r0) forbids it. A domain is
# never empty, so the ontology is inconsistent. HermiT (InconsistentOntologyException),
# JFact (via robot) and rustdl say inconsistent. Konclude v0.7.0-1138 writes a consistent
# hierarchy, but only when a named individual is declared: without the
# NamedIndividual declaration it answers inconsistent. This is one of two shapes behind the
# 21 Konclude-consistent/HermiT-inconsistent control cases: 5 are this one, 16 are an ABox role
# assertion breaking Asymmetric/Irreflexive/DisjointObjectProperties (through the role
# hierarchy), plus one EquivalentClasses(C ObjectComplementOf(C)); all 21 declare an individual.
# The generated net keeps "both peers must agree", so these are peer-disagree, never scored:
# such inconsistencies are a blind spot of the net.
Prefix(:=<http://gen.rustdl/o#>)
Prefix(owl:=<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>)
Ontology(<http://gen.rustdl/o>
Declaration(Class(:C0))
Declaration(ObjectProperty(:r0))
Declaration(NamedIndividual(:a0))
AsymmetricObjectProperty(:r0)
ReflexiveObjectProperty(:r0)
)
